#define a 1
^f00Of course I miss you, darlin'.

#define a 2
^f00This is the loneliest place on earth.

#define a 3
^f00Most exciting thing ever happens here is a day when it don't rain.

#define a 4
^f00What the heck is that?

#define a 5
^f00Scuse me, darlin', I got some work to do.

#define a 6
^f00Get on in here, Pete!

#define a 7
^f00We got us a big ol' asteroid on a three-week collision course with Earth!

#define a 8
^f00The asteroid has been named Attila, after the war leader of the Huns, who devastated Europe just before the fall of the Roman Empire.

#define a 9
^f00Attila was first spotted in a tracking station in Borneo.

#define a 10
^f00According to NASA sources, the probability of impact with Earth is 99 percent.

#define a 11
^f00Five.  Four.  Ignition.  Two.  One.

#define a 12
^f00The shuttle is up and away.

#define a 13
^f00This is not a mission the shuttle was designed for, but as mission commander Boston Low said in the press conference last night,

#define a 14
^f00'If the shuttle is the last hope of the human race --'

#define a 15
^f00^c009If the shuttle is the last hope of the human race, then it'll HAVE to do the job, won't it?

#define a 16
^f00Commander Low!  Captain Low!  Boston!

#define a 17
^f00^c009Wait a minute, folks.

#define a 18
^f00^c009Let me introduce the landing team.

#define a 19
^f00^c009Ludger Brink is a noted geologist.

#define a 20
^f00^c009He'll evaluate our data on placement of the nuclear devices.

#define a 21
^f00^c012We have to be accurate.

#define a 22
^f00^c012The idea isn't to blow Attila to bits.

#define a 23
^f00^c012If we did, some of the pieces would certainly hit Earth with devastating effect.

#define a 24
^f00^c012We must move the asteroid out of its collision course into Earth orbit.

#define a 25
^f00^c009And now I hardly have to introduce Maggie Robbins to YOU.

#define a 26
^f00^c009She's probably the most well-known journalist in the world.

#define a 27
^f00Maggie, you're famous for having once said that you'd NEVER put up with censorship in any form.

#define a 28
^f00Now you're under NASA command --

#define a 29
^f00^c009Miss Robbins is a reporter by vocation, but on this mission she's --

#define a 30
^f00^c014I think I can answer the question myself, Commander Low.

#define a 31
^f00^c014Danny, I trained for this mission and I have work to do in laying the nuclear charges.

#define a 32
^f00^c014When I come home, I'll be a reporter and tell you all about it.

#define a 33
^f00^c014But during the mission, I'm part of the team and I will obey Commander Low like any good soldier.

#define a 34
^f00That may be the biggest news story of all -- Maggie Robbins obeys orders!

#define a 35
^f00Roomful of laughter

#define a 36
^f00In going over your bios, I find that Professor Brink is also a noted archaeologist, while it's well-known that Maggie is a prodigy at learning new languages.

#define a 37
^f00Is this just coincidence?

#define a 38
^f00^c009Not at all.

#define a 39
^f00^c009We wanted the best and the brightest for this mission.

#define a 40
^f00^c009Dr. Brink and Ms. Robbins are not narrow specialists.

#define a 41
^f00^c009They are resourceful, widely educated, and creative thinkers.

#define a 42
^f00Does that apply to you, too, Commander Low?

#define a 43
^f00^c009My job is to keep everybody alive.

#define a 44
^f00^c009I don't have to be brilliant, I just have to be careful.

#define a 45
^f00More laughter.

#define a 46
^f00Good job of keeping the lid on the secret aspects of the mission in that press conference, Commander Low.

#define a 47
^f00^c009That's why I get the big bucks, General.

#define a 48
^f00Attila was out there for years, a strange duck but not dangerous, and then suddenly it was headed straight for Earth.

#define a 49
^f00SOMETHING made it change course.

#define a 50
^f00At the first evidence of alien intelligence, you clamp down the lid, Low.

#define a 51
^f00You understand?

#define a 52
^f00^c009The other two crew members will remain with the shuttle.

#define a 53
^f00^c009Ken Borden is the most experienced shuttle pilot we have.

#define a 54
^f00^c009Cora Miles is our payload specialist.

#define a 55
^f00^c009As you all know, she's a candidate for Congress, but we figured saving the planet is more important than campaigning.

#define a 56
^f00^c011It's cheaper, too.

#define a 57
^f00Laughter.

#define a 58
^f00^c009Folks, it's time for us to go.

#define a 59
^f00Any parting message for the people of Earth?

#define a 60
^f00^c009We have exactly one chance.

#define a 61
^f00^c009We've got to do it right.

#define a 62
^f00^c009Let all your prayers be with us.

